  'desc.opencolor': 'Open-source 13 hues × 10 steps tuned for UI; greys and colors designed together, great in both themes.',
  'desc.tailwind': '22 hues × 11 steps (50–950); the most-used default palette on the web, maps directly to Tailwind class names.',
  'desc.antd': 'Ant Design system palette: 12 hues × 10 steps with official dark variants, generated by their algorithm — primary sits at step 6.',
  'desc.radix': 'All 31 hues × 12 steps with explicit semantics (1-2 backgrounds / 5-7 borders / 9-10 accents / 11-12 text); native light+dark pairs, the de-facto a11y standard.',
  'desc.material2': 'Google\u2019s classic MD palette: 18 hues × 10 steps plus accent series — a decade of Android/Google standard; 500 is the primary.',
  'desc.material3': 'The core of M3 dynamic color: 6 tonal palettes × 13 tones generated in HCT space — tone 40 ≈ primary, tone 80 ≈ dark-theme primary, tone 10 ≈ text on dark.',
  'desc.carbon': 'IBM\u2019s official token palette: 14 families × 10 steps (x0 lightest → x100 darkest), rigorous and even — the enterprise benchmark (iconic blue = blue60).',
  'desc.colorbrewer-seq': 'The cartography classic by Cynthia Brewer — sequential: single-hue ramps for magnitude data, most schemes marked colorblind & print safe.',
  'desc.colorbrewer-div': 'The cartography classic — diverging: center-out transitions for deviation data, most schemes marked colorblind & print safe.',
  'desc.colorbrewer-qual': 'The cartography classic — qualitative: hue-jumping category colors, most schemes marked colorblind & print safe.',
  'desc.nord': 'A 16-color arctic theme: Polar Night depths, Snow Storm foregrounds, Frost blues and Aurora accents — the clean dark-UI classic.',
  'desc.dracula': 'Deep purple base with high-voltage neon accents; instantly recognizable, ported to 300+ editors and apps.',
  'desc.solarized': 'A meticulously calibrated 16-color system serving both dark (base03) and light (base3) modes from the same values.',
  'desc.catppuccin-latte': 'The light flavor of the low-saturation “catppuccino” theme, ported to hundreds of apps.',
  'desc.catppuccin-frappe': 'A mid-dark flavor of the low-saturation “catppuccino” theme.',
  'desc.catppuccin-macchiato': 'A darker flavor of the low-saturation “catppuccino” theme.',
  'desc.catppuccin-mocha': 'The darkest flavor of the low-saturation “catppuccino” theme, ported to hundreds of apps.',
  'desc.nippon': 'About 250 Japanese traditional color names (romaji + kanji) with values — refined and restrained.',
  'desc.mpl-viridis': 'Perceptually uniform, colorblind-friendly default sequential map — deep purple to bright yellow; superb on dark backgrounds.',
  'desc.mpl-plasma': 'Viridis’ warmer sibling: deep purple → magenta → orange → bright yellow.',
  'desc.mpl-inferno': 'Black → purple → red → orange → bright yellow, blackbody-like — great for heat data.',
  'desc.mpl-magma': 'Softer than Inferno: black → purple-pink → orange → pale yellow.',
  'desc.mpl-cividis': 'Blue-yellow sequential map optimized for red-green colorblindness — nearly no distortion for either type.',
  'desc.mpl-turbo': 'Google’s improved rainbow — more even than jet, but prefer the Viridis family in publications.',
  'desc.mpl-twilight': 'Cyclic: white → blue → black → blue → white; ideal for angles and phases.',
  'desc.mpl-managua': 'Cyclic (Crameri managua in matplotlib): green-white-purple closed loop.',
  'desc.mpl-berlin': 'Cyclic: black → blue → green → white → black — great for phase wheels.',
  'desc.mpl-vanimo': 'Cyclic (Crameri vanimo): red-grey-blue closed loop, colorblind-friendly.',
